            <ArticleTitle>The use of a three-dimensional print model of an aortic arch to plan a complex percutaneous intervention in a patient with coarctation of the aorta.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1568-1572</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S1047951116001827</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recently, three-dimensional printing of heart models is being used to plan percutaneous and surgical interventions in patients with CHD. We describe a case where we used a three-dimensional print model to plan a complex percutaneous intervention in a patient with coarctation of the aorta.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
